recommendations.detail:
styles.css line 5 currently does `@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/...')`. That creates a serial chain before any text can render: HTML, then styles.css, then Google's CSS, then the woff2 files.

Fix:
1. Download Prata 400 and Open Sans as WOFF2 files, Latin subset only. Open Sans can be the variable file or just 400 and 600.
2. Put them in assets/fonts and declare them at the top of styles.css:
```css
@font-face{font-family:'Prata';src:url(../fonts/prata-400-latin.woff2) format('woff2');font-weight:400;font-display:swap;unicode-range:U+0000-00FF,U+0131,U+0152-0153,U+02BB-02BC,U+02C6,U+02DA,U+02DC,U+2000-206F,U+2074,U+20AC,U+2122,U+2191,U+2193,U+2212,U+2215,U+FEFF,U+FFFD}
@font-face{font-family:'Open Sans';src:url(../fonts/opensans-var-latin.woff2) format('woff2');font-weight:400 600;font-display:swap;unicode-range:(same)}
@font-face{font-family:'Prata Fallback';src:local('Georgia');size-adjust:105%;ascent-override:90%;descent-override:24%;line-gap-override:0%}
@font-face{font-family:'Open Sans Fallback';src:local('Arial');size-adjust:105.1%;ascent-override:101.1%;descent-override:27.7%;line-gap-override:0%}
:root{--serif:'Prata','Prata Fallback',Georgia,serif;--sans:'Open Sans','Open Sans Fallback',Arial,sans-serif}
```
The override percentages above are starting points. Compute the real ones with Fontaine or the capsizecss metrics.
3. Preload only the font the hero headline uses: `<link rel="preload" href="assets/fonts/prata-400-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>`.
4. Drop weight 300 for body text. At 16px, #6b6b6b in 300 weight reads very thin on phones. Use 400.
5. Prata has no italic. Requesting `ital@0;1` returns only the normal style, so the mockup's italic headline word would be a faked, slanted oblique. Either set the accent word upright in --gold-text (or --gold-dk at 24px+), or add one real italic display face as a deliberate addition.

If you stay on the Google CDN, at least move it to a `<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>` plus a `<link rel="stylesheet">` in `<head>` instead of @import.

The current `.field input:focus{outline:1px solid var(--gold)}` is a 1px ring at 2.73:1 and fails. There is no global focus style.

Replace it with:
```css
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold-dk);outline-offset:3px;border-radius:2px}
.band--dark :focus-visible,.topbar :focus-visible{outline-color:var(--gold)}
.on-photo :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #fff;box-shadow:0 0 0 6px var(--ink)}
input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold-dk);outline-offset:1px}
html{scroll-padding-top:calc(var(--header-h) + 16px);scroll-padding-bottom:calc(var(--bookbar-h,0px) + 16px)}
```
Contrast of these rings:
- --gold-dk ring: 3.78 on white, 3.57 on cream.
- --gold ring on the dark band: 6.24.
- The white-plus-ink double ring stays visible on any photo.

The scroll-padding keeps focused elements from sliding under a sticky header or the mobile sticky 'Book' bar. Never write `outline:none` without a replacement.

Rules:
- Every nav link, footer link, social icon, carousel control, dialog close button and filter chip must be at least 24x24 CSS px, or have 24px of clear space around it.
- Aim for at least 44px on Book, Call, Directions and the mobile menu button.

CSS:
```css
.footer-links a,.topbar a{display:inline-block;padding-block:10px;min-height:44px;line-height:24px}
.social a{width:44px;height:44px}
.bio-close{min-width:44px;min-height:44px}
.btn{min-height:48px;padding:14px 28px}
```
The top bar (address, phone, gift cards, socials) is the most likely failure. Tiny uppercase links packed together need padding or gap.

Links inside paragraphs are exempt, but they must be underlined. They are currently distinguished only by gold color, and gold against #6b6b6b body text is about 1.0:1, which fails 1.4.1 Use of Color:
```css
.prose a{color:var(--gold-text);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-thickness:1px}
```

Build motion as an opt-in and turn it off under `reduce`:
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference){
  html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
  .reveal{opacity:0;transform:translateY(12px);transition:opacity .6s,transform .6s}
  .reveal.is-in{opacity:1;transform:none}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
  *,*::before,*::after{animation-duration:.01ms!important;animation-iteration-count:1!important;transition-duration:.01ms!important;scroll-behavior:auto!important}
}
```
In JS:
```js
const rm = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
```
Use `rm` to skip autoplay and to pass `behavior: rm ? 'auto' : 'smooth'` to scrollTo. The current back-to-top button always smooth-scrolls.

Animate only transform and opacity, never top, left or height. Content hidden by scroll-reveal must still show if JS fails: add the `.reveal` class from JS, not in the HTML.

On phones, a bottom bar with Book Now (primary, gold fill with ink text) and Call (tel:740-366-1604) keeps the conversion action in reach on long pages:
```css
.bookbar{position:fixed;inset:auto 0 0 0;display:flex;gap:8px;padding:8px 16px calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);z-index:60}
.bookbar a{flex:1;min-height:48px;display:grid;place-items:center}
@media (min-width:900px){.bookbar{display:none}}
body{padding-bottom:calc(64px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))}
```
Set `--bookbar-h` for the scroll-padding-bottom in the focus rule. Show the phone number as visible text too, not only as a tel: link. Render the bar in the static partial so it causes no layout shift.
